.TH LN 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
ln \- link files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ln
.RB [ \-fs ]
.I source_file target_file
.br
.B ln
.RB [ \-fs ]
.I source_file
.RI [ source_file ]\ .\|.\|.
.I target_dir
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ln
creates a link named
.I target_file
that refers to
.IR source_file .
By default the link is a hard link (see
.BR \-s
below).
.PP
If more than one
.I source_file
is given, or a single
.I source_file
is given together with a final operand that already exists as a
directory, each
.I source_file
is linked into that directory under its own final pathname component.
.PP
Without
.BR \-f ,
if the destination pathname already exists,
.B ln
leaves it untouched, writes a diagnostic, and continues with any
remaining
.I source_file
operands rather than creating that one link.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
If the destination pathname already exists (checked without following
a symbolic link at that name, so an existing dangling symbolic link
still counts), remove it first so the link can be created in its
place.
.TP
.B \-s
Create a symbolic link instead of a hard link. The
.B \-f
and
.B \-s
options may be combined in one argument (for example
.BR \-fs )
or given separately.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-P
Not implemented. Each must be given as its own, separate argument to
be recognized as one of these options at all; when given that way,
.B ln
prints a diagnostic and exits immediately with status 1 rather than
guess which of a symbolic-link source's two identities \(em the link
itself, or the file it resolves to \(em a hard link should be made
to. Neither flag given is equivalent to
.BR \-P .
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I source_file
A pathname naming the existing file (or, with
.BR \-s ,
any pathname, existing or not) that the new link refers to.
.TP
.I target_file
A pathname for the new link, used in the exactly-one-source form.
.TP
.I target_dir
A pathname of an existing directory, used when linking one or more
source operands into it under their own basenames.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every operand was linked successfully.
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred: an invalid option, a missing operand, or a failure
creating one or more of the requested links. In the exactly-one-source
form this stops immediately; in the multiple-source/target_dir form,
a failure on one source does not stop the rest from being attempted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cp (1),
.BR rm (1),
.BR readlink (1)
